$$\begin{aligned}
L & =I \omega \text { and } \omega=\frac{L}{I} \\
\omega & =\frac{L}{m\left(\frac{2 d}{3}\right)^{2}+2 m\left(\frac{d}{3}\right)^{2}}=\frac{L}{\frac{4}{9} m d^{2}+\frac{2}{9} m d^{2}}=\frac{L}{\frac{6 m d^{2}}{9}} \\
\omega & =\frac{3 L}{2 m d^{2}}
\end{aligned}$$

Current is maximum, so resonance and $\omega=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\text { LC }}}$
$$\begin{array}{l}
\mathrm{C}=\frac{1}{\omega^{2} \mathrm{~L}}=\frac{1}{2 \times 10^{4}} \\
=50 \times 10^{-6}=50 \mu \mathrm{~F}
\end{array}$$

$$\begin{array}{l}
\mathrm{C}_{1}=\frac{5 \in_{0} \mathrm{~A} / 2}{\mathrm{~d} / 2}=\frac{5 \in_{0} \mathrm{~A}}{\mathrm{~d}}=5 \mathrm{C} \\
\mathrm{C}_{2}=\frac{2 \in_{0} \mathrm{~A} / 2}{\mathrm{~d} / 2}=\frac{2 \in_{0} \mathrm{~A}}{\mathrm{~d}}=2 \mathrm{C}
\end{array}$$
$\mathrm{C}_{1} \& \mathrm{C}_{2}$ in series.
$$\begin{array}{l}
\mathrm{C}^{\prime}=\frac{\mathrm{C}_{1} \mathrm{C}_{2}}{\mathrm{C}_{1}+\mathrm{C}_{2}}=\frac{(5 \mathrm{C})(2 \mathrm{C})}{7 \mathrm{C}}=\frac{10}{7} \mathrm{C} \\
\mathrm{C}_{3}=\frac{3 \in_{0} \mathrm{~A} / 2}{\mathrm{~d} / 2}=3 \mathrm{C} \\
\mathrm{C}_{4}=\frac{2 \in_{0} \mathrm{~A} / 2}{\mathrm{~d} / 2}=2 \mathrm{C}
\end{array}$$
$\mathrm{C}_{4} \& \mathrm{C}_{3}$ in series; $\mathrm{C}^{\prime \prime}=\frac{(2 \mathrm{C})(3 \mathrm{C})}{5 \mathrm{C}}=\frac{6}{5} \mathrm{C}$
C' \& C'' in parallel;
So, $\mathrm{C}_{\mathrm{eq}}=\mathrm{C}\left(\frac{6}{5}+\frac{10}{7}\right)=\mathrm{C}\left(\frac{42+50}{35}\right)=\left(\frac{92}{35}\right) \mathrm{C}$
$$\begin{array}{l}
\frac{92}{35} C=\frac{\mathrm{nC}}{3} \\
\mathrm{n}=\frac{92 \times 3}{35}=7.9 \Rightarrow \mathrm{n} \simeq 8
